---
/** What to know around the install: requirements, first launch, updates and verifying. */
import { getLatestRelease } from '@/core/release';
import { REPO } from '@/core/site';
import { href } from '@/shared/lib/href';

const release = await getLatestRelease();
---

<div class="info-grid">
  <section class="card info prose">
    <h2>Before you install</h2>
    <p>
      Homeport manages Docker Engines — it doesn't include one. Run it next to Docker Engine, Docker
      Desktop, Colima, OrbStack, Rancher Desktop or Podman, or point it at a remote server over SSH,
      TLS or TCP.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>OS keychain</strong> (macOS Keychain, Windows Credential Manager, or a Secret
        Service such as GNOME Keyring) to store SSH keys, TLS certificates, Stack environments and
        repositories' deploy keys and tokens.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>
          <code>docker compose</code>
        </strong>{' '}
        on this machine to deploy Managed, Linked and Synced Stacks.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>
          <code>git</code>
        </strong>{' '}
        on this machine for Synced Stacks, deployed from a git repository.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All are optional: Homeport tells you what is unavailable without them. See the{' '}
      <a href={href('/docs/requirements/')}>system requirements</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card info prose">
    <h2>First launch</h2>
    <p>
      The installers are not yet signed with a paid certificate, so your system may ask for
      confirmation once:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Windows</strong>: SmartScreen shows “Windows protected your PC”. Choose{' '}
        <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>macOS</strong>: if Homeport “can't be opened”, allow it in{' '}
        <em>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security</em> and choose <em>Open Anyway</em>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href={href('/docs/installation/')}>Step-by-step instructions</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card info prose">
    <h2>Staying up to date</h2>
    <p>
      On Windows, macOS and with the AppImage, Homeport tells you when a new version is out and
      installs it when you choose. Every update is signed and checked before it's installed.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <code>.deb</code> and <code>.rpm</code> packages update with the rest of your system, from
      the Homeport package repository.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={href('/docs/reference/updating/')}>How updates work</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card info prose">
    <h2>Verify your download</h2>
    <p>
      Every release is built by GitHub Actions from the public source, with a SHA-256 checksum and a
      signed build provenance attestation for each file.
    </p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>gh attestation verify &lt;file&gt; --repo {REPO}</code></pre>
    <p>
      {release?.checksumsUrl ? (
        <a href={release.checksumsUrl}>SHA256SUMS.txt</a>
      ) : (
        <span>SHA256SUMS.txt</span>
      )}{' '}
      · <a href={href('/docs/reference/verifying/')}>How to verify</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .info-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 26rem), 1fr));
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  /* Outrank .prose from the global stylesheet rather than tie with it. */
  .info.prose {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .info.prose h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .info ul {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .info .code-block {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
</style>
